{
  "id": "u04-l03",
  "unit": "u04-food",
  "title": "I eat, you eat",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Your first full verb. The stem is **খা-** (*kha-*) and the ending shows who:\n\n- আমি / আমরা → **খাই** (*khai*)\n- তুই / তোরা → **খাস** (*khash*)\n- তুমি / তোমরা → **খাও** (*khao*)\n- আপনি / তিনি / উনি → **খান** (*khan*)\n- সে / ও / তারা → **খায়** (*khay*)\n\nPolite forms end in **-ন**, and polite 'you' = polite 'he/she': **তিনি মাছ খান** (polite) but **সে মাছ খায়**.\n\nBengali 'eats' drinks too: **আমি চা খাই** = 'I drink tea'.\n\nFor 'don't', put **না** *after* the verb: **আমি মাংস খাই না** = 'I don't eat meat.' (Not নেই, which means 'there isn't'.) Word order is subject – object – verb: আমি ভাত খাই = 'I rice eat.'",
  "vocab": [
